## UI Validation Kit

This project has the [UI Validation Kit](https://github.com/Dallionking/ui-validation-kit) installed.

### What's available

- **Skill:** `ui-validation` — click-through validation for iOS Simulator, Android emulator, and web. Auto-loads on triggers like "validate the app", "screenshot the UI", "test buttons work".
- **Sub-agent:** `qa-validator` — full validation runs with cost-tiered fix triage, multi-platform sweep, structured reporting.

### When to use

- Quick smoke check ("does the home screen render?") → use the `ui-validation` skill in-line
- Full validation run ("QA every screen", "test all interactions") → dispatch the `qa-validator` sub-agent
- After any UI change to confirm nothing regressed → trigger `ui-validation`

### Tooling installed

| Platform | Primary | Optional / fallback |
|---|---|---|
| iOS / Android / tvOS / desktop | `agent-device` (Callstack — one CLI, `@eN` refs) + Maestro + Maestro Viewer | `xcrun simctl`, `adb`, ios-simulator-mcp, XcodeBuildMCP, mobile-mcp |
| Web | `agent-browser` (Vercel Labs — `@eN` refs, Web Vitals, React DevTools) | Playwright MCP, Chrome DevTools MCP |

### Behavior rules

- **Click-through only** — never type URL paths to navigate after initial launch
- **Fix-before-moving-on, cost-tiered** — cheap fixes in-flight, expensive ones escalate to findings
- **Evidence-based reporting** — every PASS/FAIL cites a screenshot or video timestamp
- **Platform-aware install** — only the MCPs for detected platforms are active

See `.agents/skills/ui-validation/SKILL.md` for the full skill and `.codex/agents/qa-validator.toml` for the sub-agent.
